# GNU adns 1.0 — our delta from pristine upstream.
#
# Upstream: https://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~ian/adns/ftp/adns-1.0.tar.gz
#           sha256 bed27a4ec5b71acc08333368e842a1248e83328018b582caf644985539967c5d
# Apply from sdk/lib/3rdparty/adns/ with: patch -p1 < vendor-patches/adns.patch
#
# READ THIS FIRST: the delta is NOT ours. It is overwhelmingly a THIRD-PARTY WINDOWS
# PORT that arrived already applied — "the ADNS resolver library for Windows, ported by
# Jarle (jgaa) Aase", per adns_win32/README.TXT, built here with -DADNS_JGAA_WIN32.
# Exactly ONE file in the whole tree carries a __REACTOS__ marker (src/setup.c), so
# treating this diff as ReactOS's work would be wrong.
#
# Version is 1.0 and is certain: every top-level file (COPYING, GPL-vs-LGPL, README,
# INSTALL, TODO, changelog, configure.in, acconfig.h, aclocal.m4, Makefile.in,
# settings.make.in, install-sh) is byte-identical to pristine adns-1.0, and the changelog's
# newest entry is "adns (1.0)".
#
# THE PORT'S OWN UPSTREAM IS GONE. adns.jgaa.com does not resolve (jgaa.com itself still
# does) and the Wayback API returns no snapshot, so there is no artifact to diff the port
# against — the same dead-distribution problem as dxtn. That is why this patch is taken
# against GNU adns 1.0 rather than against the port: it is the only surviving reference
# point, so the hunks below conflate "jgaa's port" with "any later local change". Do not
# read a hunk here as a ReactOS decision without checking for a __REACTOS__ marker first.
#
# NORMALIZE BEFORE YOU COUNT. This tree is CRLF in places and a raw diff badly overstates
# it: src/adns.h is 150 raw changed lines but 92 real ones, src/types.c 115 raw vs 51.
#
# SCOPE — only src/ is compiled (plus adns_win32/adns_unix_calls.c):
#   src/       11 files, ~570 normalized lines. COMPILED. This is the port proper.
#   client/    8 files, ~123 normalized lines. NOT COMPILED — the adnshost/adnslogres
#              command-line tools are not in our CMake source list. Included here only so
#              that pristine + patch reproduces the tree exactly.
#
# NOT IN THIS PATCH (no upstream counterpart — the port ADDS these):
#   adns_win32/adns_unix_calls.c, adns_win32.h   GPL-2.0-or-later, jgaa + Ian Jackson.
#                                                adns_unix_calls.c IS compiled.
#   adns_win32/timercmp.h
#   adns_win32/getopt.c, getopt.h   *** DELETED 2026-09-20 — unlicensed dead code ***
#       getopt.c's header said verbatim: "jgaa oct 9th 2000: Found this on www. No
#       copyright information given. Slightly modified." with an origin URL on
#       winsite.com. Carrying a file whose licence is "none stated" is exactly the
#       provenance hole this registry exists to close, so both files are gone.
#       They were never in the CMake source list. NOTE the one referrer, so nobody is
#       surprised later: client/adnslogres.c does `#include "getopt.h"` under
#       ADNS_JGAA_WIN32 — but client/ appears NOWHERE in our CMakeLists, so the whole
#       adnshost/adnslogres tool set is already unbuilt vendored source. Reviving those
#       tools now needs a getopt from somewhere with a licence; that is a feature.
#
